<title>BRAZIL: Brazil lower house delays labor contract vote.</title>
<headline>Brazil lower house delays labor contract vote.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>A vote by the Brazilian Chamber of Deputies on a bill creating a new temporary labor contract has been postponed until Wednesday, a government whip said.</p>
<p>Deputy Benito Gama, the government leader in the lower house, gave no reason for the delay.</p>
<p>The temporary labor contract would allow employers to hire temporary staff for a maximum of two years, paying reduced worker contributions. The government hopes the bill will help reduce unemployment.</p>
<p>-- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom, 5561 2230358</p>
</text>
